-- title:
--   Finiteness of the vertex orbit space for away-units
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ with $a<0$ and $b<0$, so that $\mathbb{H} = \mathrm{\mathbb{H}}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is the quaternion algebra with the given structure constants, and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ satisfying `IsOrder R`, that is: $1 \in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and $R$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. a finite place. Consider the vertex set `CosetGraph.Vert R v`, the quotient of the unit group of the local algebra `Loc a b v` by the subgroup `level R v` generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) together with `scalarUnits v`; and the group `CosetGraph.awayUnits R v` of those units of $\mathbb{H}$ whose image under `toLoc w` lies in the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) for every finite place $w \neq v$. This group acts on `Vert R v`, and `CosetGraph.ProjAwayUnits R v` is its quotient by the kernel `actionKer R v` of the associated permutation representation, so that the quotient group acts faithfully. The assertion is that the orbit space of this action, `Mumford.QuotVert (CosetGraph.ProjAwayUnits R v) (CosetGraph.Vert R v)`, is finite.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the quotient of the vertex set of the Bruhat–Tits tree at $v$ by the projective away-unit group of an order in a definite rational quaternion algebra, the cocompactness statement underlying the finiteness of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient graph; classically it is deduced from the finiteness of the adelic class set of the order. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd), where finitely many orbit representatives of vertices are extracted together with finiteness of vertex stabilisers.
-- source:
